{
  "design_decisions": [
    "The examples-only config contains no path to either successful adapter weights or the reconstructed generator. No reconstruction loss or teacher outputs are used.",
    "Heads/fixed-RTE changes exactly the component set of the successful construction: input/output alignment and shared A/B affine heads. Hidden network, original task vectors, and layer embeddings remain frozen.",
    "Heads/new-latents and full/new-latents train the new ABC vectors and layer embeddings, while preserving all original task vectors exactly. Each is compared with a rank8 LoRA initialized from the same released RTE factors.",
    "Target calibration uses actual constructed core plus fixed original RTE vector for all ABC tasks; untouched source uses the same RTE routing. Fresh target maps and layer embeddings match exactly before optimization. Shared core and every latent remain frozen.",
    "Use three task microbatches of four examples per update with EMA-normalized gold-answer token NLL. Data, updates and rank match; parameter counts do not.",
    "Check finite gradients by component family, zero gradients before extra updates, actual update/exposure counts including failed updates, and generated factor RMS and full B@A update norms. Nonfinite/zero-gradient arms stop and return a diagnostic so the runner can continue other arms.",
    "A single zero B path is deliberate. A double-zero output/head initialization receives zero gradients; a CPU test confirms it stops with zero optimizer updates.",
    "All old-task retention questions are from the exact saved prior catalog selection: 32 each of BoolQ, HellaSwag, WinoGrande, CommonsenseQA. Native retains original task routing; persistent LoRA has its own baseline and cannot be compared with unmatched absolute task-adapter starting scores.",
    "The old validation rows are intentionally monitored. Old test, exhaustive-triple, and sealed length4 evaluations occur after every arm finishes training, in a distinct PID. No holdout-based checkpoint selection. Previously exposed triples are reported as exploratory.",
    "The zero-start config changes both initialization and learning rate relative to the conservative released-initialization config. A success there would not isolate which of those changes helped.",
    "Length4 is a fresh length-generalization panel on known mappings. It is not free generation, a new task mapping, or a sustained-learning result."
  ],
